---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RoadmapCard from '@/components/RoadmapCard.astro';
import { roadmap, statusUpdated, testing } from '@/data/development';
---
<BaseLayout title="Playtest Status · Spirebreak" description="What is in the current Spirebreak playtest build, what feedback is most useful and which parts still need work.">
  <section class="page-hero shell">
    <span class="eyebrow">PLAYTEST STATUS</span>
    <h1>What to look for in your next run.</h1>
    <p>The current build includes Tier III weapon mutations and Resonance opportunities that can connect a strong weapon to a larger strategy. We want to know whether those moments are clear, exciting and still feel like your decisions.</p>
    <small>Updated <time datetime={statusUpdated}>September 21, 2026</time></small>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">IN THE CURRENT BUILD</span>
      <h2>The parts that need the most player feedback.</h2>
      <p>These systems are playable now, but their clarity, balance and feel can still change.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid two">{roadmap.filter((item) => item.lane === 'now').map((item) => <RoadmapCard {...item} />)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="eyebrow">AFTER YOUR RUN</span>
      <h2>Four questions worth answering.</h2>
      <p>You do not need numbers or a formal report. The moment that felt great, confusing or unfair is often the most useful feedback.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="test-grid">{testing.map((item, index) => <article class="test-item"><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.question}</p></div></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell methodology">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">WHAT YOUR FEEDBACK CHANGES</span>
      <h2>Tell us about the decisions, not just the result.</h2>
      <p>A win can still feel flat. A loss can still make you eager to try a better plan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-grid">
      <article><strong>What you chose</strong><p>Which weapon, mutation or Artifact changed your plan, and which offers never felt worth buying?</p></article>
      <article><strong>What stopped you</strong><p>Tell us which enemy, boss attack or unclear rule ended the run or forced you to adapt.</p></article>
      <article><strong>What you want to try next</strong><p>The build you almost completed tells us more about replayability than a simple win rate.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
